# p2-ascent.drv - Phase 2 tour: lift off from an atmospheric surface port
# under an overcast and climb nose-up out of the sky into space.
#
# Verifies: clouds2 (W5b2) the sky deck seen from the pad and from below,
# and that it stays when the nose comes up so far that the horizon leaves
# the picture: the game then sends no planet at all, and the deck is drawn
# on from the last one (deck_hook, docs/hd/clouds.md).  Then the deck from
# above and the hand-over to the orbit view of the clouds.
# Run:  tools/p2shots --routes ascent --base BASE --branch BRANCH
# The sky over this port is clear on the first afternoon, so the route
# first runs the clock at 10000x to midnight (the port's midnight message
# drops it to 1x, which fixes the start), then 65 s at 1000x to about
# 18:00 on the second day, when the port is under an overcast.  The .drv
# language has no verb that waits on game state, so these are waits on
# wall time; a busy machine moves the clock a little.
# Expect: 01 the pad (external view) under the overcast, 02 the front view
#         just after lift-off (the deck overhead, the horizon in view),
#         03 nose up under thrust (the horizon low in the picture), 04 and
#         05 nose far up, the horizon gone (base: an empty sky; branch: the
#         deck, thinning at 04 as the ship comes up to its height, and gone
#         at 05, above it), 06 the rear view, 07 high (at 10x), 08 space.
#         The frames across the horizon leaving are the proof of the hook:
#         record them with a frame dump, not these shots.
# Each shot pauses the game (Esc) and resumes it at 1x (Shift+F1); the
# pointer is parked off the controls so no hover tip is drawn.
# Log markers: padtime..padend (landed, for frame timing), climb..climbend
# (the nose-up climb with the horizon out of the picture, no pauses).

wait 6000
key space
wait 2000
key 2             # start position 2: landed at a surface port with an atmosphere
wait 11000
mouse 2 120
wait 300
sdlkey f5 shift   # 10000x: on to the midnight message (1x)
wait 15000
sdlkey f4 shift   # 1000x: to about 18:00 on the second day
wait 65000
sdlkey f1 shift   # 1x
mouse 8 193       # the view icon twice: the external view
wait 300
click 200
wait 1200
mouse 8 193
wait 300
click 200
wait 1200
mouse 2 120
log padtime
wait 15000
log padend
sdlkey esc
wait 600
shot 01-pad
sdlkey f1 shift
mouse 8 193       # the view icon again: the front view
wait 300
click 200
wait 1200
mouse 57 193      # comms: ask for launch clearance
wait 300
click 200
wait 2500
mouse 171 57
wait 300
click 200
wait 3000
mouse 263 193     # lift off
wait 300
click 200
wait 2000
mouse 2 120
wait 7000
sdlkey esc
wait 600
shot 02-low
sdlkey f1 shift
press right       # a first pull: the nose up, the horizon still in view
move 0 8 6 40
release right
wait 500
keydown return    # full thrust
wait 3000
sdlkey esc
wait 600
shot 03-noseup
sdlkey f1 shift
press right       # a second pull: the horizon leaves the picture
move 0 8 10 60
release right
log climb
wait 6000
log climbend
sdlkey esc
wait 600
shot 04-sky
sdlkey f1 shift
press right       # further over
move 0 8 10 60
release right
wait 1500
sdlkey esc
wait 600
shot 05-sky
sdlkey f1 shift
mouse 8 193       # the view icon: the rear view
wait 300
click 200
wait 1200
mouse 2 120
wait 2000
sdlkey esc
wait 600
shot 06-rear
sdlkey f1 shift
sdlkey f2 shift   # 10x
wait 12000
sdlkey esc
wait 600
shot 07-high
sdlkey f1 shift
sdlkey f2 shift
wait 9000
sdlkey esc
wait 600
shot 08-space
quit
